<description>
Copy the rare-colored motif into every same-parity cell of the scaffold grid.

Input structure
- The background surrounds one scaffold color that forms full horizontal and vertical separator lines.
- A second foreground color appears only as a small motif inside one open scaffold cell.

Rule
- Split rows and columns into open cells between the full scaffold separator lines.
- Find the open cell containing all motif pixels and record those pixels as offsets from that cell's upper-left corner.
- Stamp those offsets into every open cell whose row-cell index and column-cell index have the same parity as the source cell, clipping at truncated edge cells.

Key insight
- The scaffold turns the grid into a checkerboard of cells; the seed motif marks which parity class should receive copies.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "summary": "Repeat the rare-color motif through same-parity cells of a scaffold grid.",
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "rare-color motif inside one open cell of the full-line scaffold",
  "dst": "open scaffold cells whose row-cell and column-cell parity match the source cell",
  "transform": "copy the motif's offsets from the source cell upper-left into each target cell; preserve scaffold and background elsewhere, clipping copies in truncated edge cells"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square, side = 3 + N*4 or 3 + N*4 - 2 (truncated); side 23-29
  colors: 3 total -- background (always 0), scaffold_color, motif_color (all distinct)
  scaffold:
    full horizontal and vertical lines of scaffold_color
    lines at positions 3, 7, 11, ... (first at 3, then every 4) [observed]
    row_lines == col_lines positions (symmetric square lattice)
    N separator lines per axis: 5-7
    creates a grid of open 3x3 cells; last cell may be 1x1 if grid is truncated
  motif:
    1 contiguous-or-disconnected shape of motif_color inside exactly 1 full (3x3) open cell
    pixel count: 4-6
    bounding box: always 3x3 (spans full cell) [observed]
    appears only in input inside the source cell; rest of grid is bg + scaffold
  output:
    motif copied into every open cell whose (row_cell_index % 2, col_cell_index % 2) matches the source cell's parity
    copies clipped at truncated edge cells (only offsets fitting within cell bounds are stamped)
    scaffold and bg elsewhere unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick N_seps in 5-7. Coin-flip truncated (grid = 3+N*4-2) or full (grid = 3+N*4). Grid is square.
    2. Choose bg=0, scaffold_color, motif_color (3 distinct colors, bg always 0).
    3. Place scaffold lines at rows/cols 3, 7, 11, ..., 3+4*(N_seps-1). Fill those full rows/cols with scaffold_color.
    4. Compute open cells. Pick a source cell (must be a full 3x3 cell, not truncated).
    5. Generate a random motif pattern of 4-6 pixels within the 3x3 cell (bbox should span 3x3).
    6. Stamp motif into all same-parity cells (clipping at truncated edges) to get the output.
    7. Input = output with all motif pixels removed except those in the source cell.
```
</generation_spec>
